     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>Is there any way to set environment variables on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361954530000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0a2vB6EI2HnmTLUQ95ILSv\">shinyapps.io</a> with a free account?  <br></div><div><br></div><div>One of the packages I&#39;m using requires an API key for a web API and it reads the key from an env var.  </div><div><br></div><div>I thought the function rsconnect::setProperty() would work, but I keep getting an error:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">rsconnect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">setProperty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;ENV_VAR&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;&lt;my-key&gt;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> appName</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;appname&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> account</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;janedoe&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#800\">#&gt; Error in authInfo$secret : $ operator is invalid for atomic vectors</span></div></div></code></div><br>Doing something wrong?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks! <br></div><div>Scott Chamberlain<br></div></div>"
